<article class="env-corollary" id="76592F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/76592F">Corollary <span data-tag="76592F">4.2.1.3</span>.</a> Let $S \rightarrow T$ and $S' \rightarrow T'$ be categorical equivalences of simplicial sets. Then the induced map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  S \star S' \rightarrow T \star T' \]
</div>
  <p> is a categorical equivalence. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from Proposition <a href="/tag/95637F" data-tag="95637F">4.2.1.2</a>, since the operation $\diamond $ has the desired property. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>